# Observability and Compliance

RULE: All events MUST include required fields per category. correlation_id on all coordination events, duration_ms on COMPLETED, stack_trace on FAILED, client_order_id on execution events.
WHY: End-to-end tracing, performance monitoring, audit trail, and regulatory compliance (FCA/MiFID II).
CODEX: 03-observability/lifecycle-events.md, 07-security/audit-logging.md

MACHINE-READABLE SSOT:
 unified-internal-contracts/events.py REQUIRED_EVENT_FIELDS
 unified-internal-contracts/schemas/audit.py EXECUTION_AUDIT, STRATEGY_AUDIT
 runtime-topology.yaml data_retention_policy, health_probes

DO:
 log_event("FAILED", metadata={"stack_trace": traceback.format_exc(), "error_category": "NETWORK", "correlation_id": corr_id})
 log_event("PROCESSING_COMPLETED", metadata={"duration_ms": elapsed, "correlation_id": corr_id})
 All execution events: include client_order_id and exchange_timestamp
 Persist audit records to GCS audit/{client_id}/{date}/{event_type}/

NEVER:
 log_event("FAILED") without stack_trace and error_category
 log_event("COMPLETED") without duration_ms
 Execution events without client_order_id
 Delete or modify audit records (append-only, immutable)
 Skip correlation_id on coordination events
